{"schemaVersion":1,"buildId":"f23bc85995440832e2b6","key":"clockbase-agent","recordId":"clockbase-agent","kind":"paper","lang":"en","title":"Autonomous AI Agents Discover Aging Interventions from Millions of Molecular Profiles","canonicalPath":"/papers/clockbase-agent/","fields":{"venue":"bioRxiv","year":2025,"yearLabel":"2023, revised 2025","status":"preprint","statusNote":null,"title":"Autonomous AI Agents Discover Aging Interventions from Millions of Molecular Profiles","authors":"K Ying, A Tyshkovskiy, A Moldakozhayev, H Wang, …, L Cong, A Regev, J Leskovec, T Wyss-Coray, VN Gladyshev","doi":"10.1101/2023.02.28.530532","link":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.02.28.530532","description":"ClockBase Agent employs specialized AI agents that autonomously reanalyze 43,602 intervention-control comparisons through multiple aging biomarkers, revealing thousands of age-modifying effects including 500+ interventions that significantly reduce biological age. We experimentally validated ouabain, demonstrating reduced frailty and improved cardiac function in aged mice.","descriptions":[{"sourceField":"liveResearch.description","text":"ClockBase Agent employs specialized AI agents that autonomously reanalyze 43,602 intervention-control comparisons through multiple aging biomarkers, revealing thousands of age-modifying effects including 500+ interventions that significantly reduce biological age. We experimentally validated ouabain, demonstrating reduced frailty and improved cardiac function in aged mice."},{"sourceField":"liveFeatured.description","text":"ClockBase Agent employs specialized AI agents that autonomously reanalyze 43,602 intervention-control comparisons, revealing 500+ interventions that significantly reduce biological age."},{"sourceField":"finding","text":"ClockBase Agent uses AI agents to reanalyze millions of public human and mouse methylation and RNA-seq samples with more than 40 aging clocks. Across 43,602 intervention-control comparisons it identified more than 500 interventions associated with lower biological age. One candidate, ouabain, slowed frailty progression, reduced neuroinflammation and improved cardiac function in aged mice."}],"abstract":null,"descriptionHeading":null,"descriptionSource":null,"pdfDocument":{"available":true,"sourceURL":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.02.28.530532","openPaperHref":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2023.02.28.530532","displayPolicy":"all-pages","rightsDecision":false,"identityDecision":false,"version":"preprint","licence":"CC-BY","pageCount":57,"renderedPages":57,"readingWidth":2048,"loupe":{"mode":"magnify-same-image","factor":2},"manifestHref":"/content/papers/clockbase-agent.json"},"pdfFigures":[{"figureNumber":1,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-01.webp","legendFirstSentence":"ClockBase Agent platform architecture and workflow.","page":33},{"figureNumber":2,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-02.webp","legendFirstSentence":"Comprehensive biological age atlas across human and mouse molecular profiles.","page":35},{"figureNumber":3,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-03.webp","legendFirstSentence":"AI agent-identified age-modifying interventions in mouse RNA-seq datasets.","page":37},{"figureNumber":4,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-04.webp","legendFirstSentence":"Systematic analysis of intervention categories and biological validation.","page":39},{"figureNumber":5,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-05.webp","legendFirstSentence":"AI agent operational workflow and multi-dimensional scoring system.","page":42},{"figureNumber":6,"href":"/assets/papers/clockbase-agent/figure-06.webp","legendFirstSentence":"Experimental validation of ouabain’s geroprotective effects in aged mice.","page":44}]},"figures":[{"key":"figure-ca1d4cafc4af12e0","recordHref":"/content/surfaces/figures/figure-ca1d4cafc4af12e0.json"},{"key":"figure-969a30d119a72c8a","recordHref":"/content/surfaces/figures/figure-969a30d119a72c8a.json"},{"key":"figure-4c1173470